      "problem": "If $f(x)$ is right-continuous at $x=3$ and $f(3)=1$, then what is $\\displaystyle{\\lim_{x\\to 3^+}} \\left(f(x)-x^2\\right)?$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $f(x)$ is right-continuous at $x=3,$ we must have\n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to 3^+} f(x)=f(3)=1.\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {3}^{+}}(f(x)-{x}^{2})=1-{3}^{2}=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
